{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review","id":1533461,"title":"W5 Adventure \"Reclamation\" Review","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-01T14:41:51-07:00","id":1533461,"title":"W5 Adventure \"Reclamation\" Review","content":"I've read the now-released-for-the-public adventure Reclamation and I wanted to share my thoughts on it.<br /> <br /> First, let's talk about the premise. On a meta-level this is very much supposed to be an introductory adventure. And it isn\u2019t just an introduction to W5 but the adventure comes with pre-gen characters and the first chapter of the adventure is an in-media-res opening-scene of action that the PCs can easily win. Story-wise the adventure is about a caern which has gone dark and nobody knows what has happened to its guarding Pack of Garou. The PCs are asked to investigate and then encounter some challenges as well as enemies that need to be defeated.<br /> <br /> Where the adventure works quite well is in how straightforward it is. The narrative milestones are well-connected and it\u2019s easy to see how things progress from point A and point B while the simplicity of the sketched-out plot makes sure that players can\u2019t get off-track very easily. It\u2019s quite obvious what the goals in any particular chapter are and what the obstacles are that need to be overcome. So as an introductory adventure it works quite well in that regard (both as in being an introduction for new players but also new STs).<br /> <br /> The biggest issue I had with the adventure is its worldbuilding. And I don\u2019t mean the W5-part here. It\u2019s the timeline of what happens when that is weird at times when you start to tug at the seams of this weave. Also, the writing on the introduced drug tells me that this was written by someone who has never dealt with drugs. Also, while I welcomed the integration of the pre-gen-characters into the adventure by having Backgrounds linked to particular NPCs within the story, I don\u2019t think the adventure really thought through the implications of these connections existing.<br /> <br /> But overall, I think it\u2019s fine. As a one-shot or an introduction, it\u2019s perfectly serviceable. Well, as long as you don\u2019t have somebody in the group who\u2019s very inquisitive, I think this works well enough to introduce someone to W5.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a gentleman\u2019s 6/10, I would say.<br /> <br /> (From here on are spoilers as I go into detail about what I described above)<ul><li>Here\u2019s the premise in its entirety: There\u2019s a section of a generic city called Noble Green. It got a veteran\u2019s hospital, then the city hit on hard times economically and a private company called Beckett\u2019s Biolabs moved in. They developed a drug called sNap. It\u2019s a highly addictive drug. The private company leaves. People keep passing around the drug as a new designer-drug and criminals are brewing up new stuff as well. There\u2019s a caern in Noble Green that has gone dark a week ago. The players investigate the caern and find out from its spirit that the Pack left to battle the Wyrm and hasn\u2019t returned. And the place where they went is the empty Veteran\u2019s Hospital that has fallen into ruin. Once they\u2019ve gone there the PC-Pack find out that the hospital is corrupted by the Wyrm. And they find one of the Garou from the caern\u2019s Pack. That surviving Garou has fallen to Hauglosk, though, and is now working together with a Bane Spirit to bring about the end of the world as quick as possible. They defeat the bad Garou, the Bane-Spirit flees or gets destroyed as well and\u2026 you get your patented W5-\u201csmall victory\u201d.</li> <li>The timeline-issue: The reason the timeline doesn\u2019t line up is mostly because of how the adventure starts. It says that the Sept-leader who is a Shadow Lord has Stormcrow-spirits to check on caerns and one week ago the spirits of the Noble Green caern have shut themselves off to the rest of the world. First of all, what happened in that week? Why wait a week? But then this whole timeline of this one Pack apparently going off on this attack on the hospital without informing anyone in the Sept\u2026? And then this drug being around long enough for Garou to know about it \u2013 but somehow nobody connected it to the hospital in all that time before? And that fall of this one bad Garou happened quite a while ago, though \u2026?</li> <li>The drug: It\u2019s called sNap and this is how it\u2019s described: \u201cUsed by \u201csnapping\u201d a smelling salts-esque packet under the nose and eyes, sNap is actually a brittle crystalline substance that creates powerful fumes inhaled by the user. It creates an almost instantaneous euphoric high that lasts for upwards of an hour, during which time the user is said to have \u201cgot snapped\u201d. It is powerfully addictive, easy to use, and surprisingly inexpensive when compared to other designer drugs.\u201d Sure\u2026 if you say so, buddy\u2026 I mean, come on! It\u2019s \u201ccrystalline\u201d but it \u201ccreates powerful fumes\u201d, you put it \u201cunder the nose and eyes\u201d and then you \u201cinhale\u201d\u2026 It\u2019s described as a \u201csmelling-salt\u201d! It\u2019s like the writer here didn\u2019t quite get how a to describe a \u201csmelling-salt\u201d-like drug. And a high of \u201cone hour\u201d! Seriously?! At least make it better than Heroin! But sure, \u201cit is powerfully addictive, easy to use and surprisingly inexpensive when compared to other designer drugs\u201d\u2026 whatever you say\u2026 This really would\u2019ve worked better if it were either far more supernatural or someone had done more research on drugs to write a more delievable description. It also feels a bit weird that the Garou know about this drug being this attempt at making humans immune to the Delirium. And it does do that \u2013 except it gives people a high for an hour, does weird things to their body (they feel pain as pleasure, for example), hallucinations and over time erodes the person\u2019s sense of reality. The opening chapter, that in-media-res action scene is the PC-Pack shutting down a criminal facility that produces sNap.</li> <li>The challenge and the pre-gens: At the beginning when the Sept-Leader chooses the PC-Pack to investigate the fallen caern, another Pack challenges them to replace them. The Sept Leader goes along with that and there\u2019s a ritualistic duel. The problem: If you use the pre-gen characters this gets really weird. You have the Pack-leader Gallowspeaker (a Black Fury Theurge) who has the Sept-Leader Stormchilde (Ahroun Shadow Lord) as a Mentor (a bit weird that this connection exists\u2026 it\u2019s just explained as Stormchilde thinking Gallowspeaker shows promise). Not only that but Pile-On (Bone Gnawer Ahroun) has a member from the Pack that challenges the PCs as a mentor (Curbstomp \u2013 Bone Gnawer). That\u2019s a bit weird. But also, I\u2019m fully on board with the challenge when the Sept Leader is clearly doing a favor for somebody close to them by picking the PC-Pack. On a positive note, though, I was glad to see that the caern hadn\u2019t been handed to the PCs after the adventure although it\u2019s a bit weird to give it to Curbstomp as the last surviving member of that rival Pack as well (they got demolished by the traitor-Garou with the help of his Bane-Spirit-ally)\u2026</li> <li>Hauglosk is weird: I guess this will always be a weird thing in W5. Depending on who\u2019s writing, Hauglosk can be anything between specifically Garou fanaticism and generally just plain insanity. Here\u2019s how the bad Garou who turned traitor Michal Stitches the Soul is described: \u201cNearly giving in to Harano as his pack, Crescent\u2019s Edge, witnesses failure after failure amidst their territory\u2019s fall into corruption, Michal began searching for new ways to serve his brethren when the Prophet of Loss began whispering to him. Now, months later, Michal has gone all the way to the other end of the spectrum, Hauglosk driving him to believe that flooding the community with sNap and the recipe for making more hastens the coming of the Apocalypse and the rebirth following from the end of the world.\u201d (This also brings up the timeline-issue again\u2026 supposedly the caern has only gone dark a week ago\u2026)</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-01T16:56:20-07:00","id":1533462,"title":"","content":"It seems like someone might have taken note of online discussions of Hauglosk and how, by the description as written, you can see the impressions of the Swords of Heimdall wall under the hasty wallpapering job.<br /> <br /> As for the chemical recreation plot line, it seems like they could have used some... (sunglasses) noble green.<br /> <br /> You know. For research purposes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-02T00:54:22-07:00","id":1533472,"title":"","content":"A couple more thoughts:<ul><li>There is mention of the Umbra but it is only perfunctory. The biggest scene is when the Pack goes into the Umbra and they talk to the spirits of the caern that has gone dark. Also, a sidebar on pg 14 highlights something I've always thought was a bit of a problem with W5: &quot;If the players are using the-generated Garou characters that came with this story, there are two characters who know this ritual: Kai Gallowspeaker and Elliot Fuller, Fairblade. If the players have created their own characters, at least one should know the rite. If this has been overlooked, the Storyteller can grant the rite to a character on an ad hoc basis.&quot; If I were to run a W5 game again, every PC would automatically know the Umbra-Rite, the Rite of Rage and the Rite of Tranquility automatically. The latter two are about raising and lowering Rage respectively and you need the first one to enter the Umbra. There's nothing fancy or interesting about making PCs use up XP to be capable of doing that. Especially the Umbra-one... It's such an essential part of WtA. Locking a PC-group out of entering that realm because nobody bought that one Rite for their PC is ridiculous. The adventure offers the right kind of advice here but this sort of thing should've occurred to the people who wrote the corebook and should've been avoided from the get-go.</li> <li>I think it's a bit of a miss that the adventure never tackles Harano/Hauglosk as a mechanic and how it interacts with the adventure and that Renown-Chagrin isn't mentioned when that's something the ST is expected to enforce.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-02T01:14:11-07:00","id":1533474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1533472#post1533472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially the Umbra-one... It's such an essential part of WtA. Locking a PC-group out of entering that realm because nobody bought that one Rite for their PC is ridiculous. The adventure offers the right kind of advice here but this sort of thing should've occurred to the people who wrote the corebook and should've been avoided from the get-go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just some speculation, but I have a feeling that this was very much intentional from a design aspect. The lead designer(s) didn't want umbral travel to be an automatic, inherent, default ability that all werewolves can do. By making it a Rite, it allows an ST to prevent characters from accessing the Umbra. So that an ST who doesn't want to have to deal with the Umbra can lock characters out from going there (&quot;Sorry, you don't have the rite and won't be able to learn it. No Umbral travel for this campaign.&quot;)<br /> <br /> This can make werewolves more friendly to crossovers or LARPs (which I think was a prime design point) by preventing them from traveling away from the &quot;real&quot; world. To be clear I don't like that, but I have a feeling that's why Umbral travel was locked behind a rite in W5, rather than being a basic part of the werewolf toolkit like it used to be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-02T01:56:15-07:00","id":1533475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1533474#post1533474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just some speculation, but I have a feeling that this was very much intentional from a design aspect. The lead designer(s) didn't want umbral travel to be an automatic, inherent, default ability that all werewolves can do. By making it a Rite, it allows an ST to prevent characters from accessing the Umbra. So that an ST who doesn't want to have to deal with the Umbra can lock characters out from going there (&quot;Sorry, you don't have the rite and won't be able to learn it. No Umbral travel for this campaign.&quot;)<br /> <br /> This can make werewolves more friendly to crossovers or LARPs (which I think was a prime design point) by preventing them from traveling away from the &quot;real&quot; world. To be clear I don't like that, but I have a feeling that's why Umbral travel was locked behind a rite in W5, rather than being a basic part of the werewolf toolkit like it used to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably what happened but I think in that case you can't include stuff like this during the final battle: &quot;This is likely going to be a tough fight, especially with the Prophet of Loss manifesting attacks from the safety of the Umbra. If one or more of the players\u2019 characters realize they can use the thin Gauntlet and Rite of Shadow Passage to attack the Psychomachiae within the Umbra, things might go easier.&quot; And then later it says if you defeat the Hauglosk Garou first, this Bane Spirit just escapes into the Umbra and disappears (unless the PCs go into the Umbra and chase the Spirit). You would really have to set the Umbra up as a separate thing that's optional. But with the amount of Spirits that are still relevant to even W5, it's hard to imagine how one would do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-02T05:48:18-07:00","id":1533478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> hastens the coming of the Apocalypse and the rebirth following from the end of the world.\u201d </div> </div> </div>But thats textbook BSD* not Hauglosk/Cult.<br /> <br /> *Or a certain no longer canon for W5 Coggie Camp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-02T07:21:58-07:00","id":1533481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1533478#post1533478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But thats textbook BSD* not Hauglosk/Cult.<br /> <br /> *Or a certain no longer canon for W5 Coggie Camp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hang on a second... You're right. The W5 corebook even describes it like that on pg 277: &quot;In this respect, Black Spiral Dancers are perverse accelerationists trying to hasten the End of It All, so that the cosmological cycle can renew.&quot;. So even when ignoring the previous editions, this doesn't quite fit. Because that description would mean the BSD in general are victims of Hauglosk as well, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-02T08:40:15-07:00","id":1533489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1533478#post1533478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But thats textbook BSD* not Hauglosk/Cult.<br /> <br /> *Or a certain no longer canon for W5 Coggie Camp.</div> </div> </div> </div>We keep seeing adventures where it really feels like they were originally written with the idea that the villain(s) were going to be Black Spiral Dancers, but then they reskinned the villain into a werewolf in hauglosk at the last minute. This has the effect of making it so that when a werewolf falls into Hauglosk, they're basically just a BSD by a different name. So off-hand, it seems to me that even the writers don't really know what the hell to do with Hauglosk or how to represent it in play, which is pretty problematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 04-02-2024, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-02T09:42:15-07:00","id":1533491,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm glad they included a wolf-born. But I have no idea why Soot and Cinder is a Hart Warden of all tribes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-02T10:00:45-07:00","id":1533492,"title":"","content":"Well, he likes music apparently and Hart Wardens are the Galliard-Tribe and Galliards are one thing above all in W5 (if the chosen archetypes in the corebook are to be believed): musicians. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-02T10:21:30-07:00","id":1533493,"title":"","content":"Also also, not only has the writer not done drug research, they ALSO haven't done ANY research on Wolfbane.<br /> <br /> Because if one PC is addicted to adderall, they sure as fuck can't deal with Acanite poisoning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-02T10:56:58-07:00","id":1533495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1533493#post1533493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also also, not only has the writer not done drug research, they ALSO haven't done ANY research on Wolfbane.<br /> <br /> Because if one PC is addicted to adderall, they sure as fuck can't deal with Acanite poisoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, most living beings have a really hard time with aconite, even if they're not on anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-02T11:04:26-07:00","id":1533496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1533495#post1533495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, most living beings have a really hard time with aconite, even if they're not on anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I just mean that in Legacy regen would make adderall addiction near impossible. So if THAT affects garou strongly in W5, it is not just Fairblade that needs to watch out with wolfsbane XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T00:24:15-07:00","id":1533506,"title":"","content":"There's another pre-gen that is a bit weird: It's Wrong Path Jensen who's a Silent Strider Ragabash with concept Graffiti Cartographer.<br /> <br /> This is how they're described: &quot;Never far from a few cans of spray paint or jars of brushon, Wrong Path turns the back alley walls and human landmarks to create a colorful map of warnings and signs to the Nation. They blame themself for not realizing sooner how bad things have fallen around this area, and frequently enact the Rite of Contrition to make up for any taint their poisonous paints might have carried with them.&quot;<br /> <br /> The character has the Rite of Contrition but it has an actual mechanic attached to it. You do it to counteract Renown-Chagrin. But the description is weird in the sense that this character apparently keeps doing graffiti but also thinks that's bad because of the environmental damage the paints are causing. Not only that, but the chances of this character succeeding on this Rite are low. Also, I don't think I would put this character into Chagrin for spray-painting a wall... Especially if the goal of the action is to set up warning-signs for other Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T00:33:44-07:00","id":1533507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1533506#post1533506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's another pre-gen that is a bit weird: It's Wrong Path Jensen who's a Silent Strider Ragabash with concept Graffiti Cartographer.<br /> <br /> This is how they're described: &quot;Never far from a few cans of spray paint or jars of brushon, Wrong Path turns the back alley walls and human landmarks to create a colorful map of warnings and signs to the Nation. They blame themself for not realizing sooner how bad things have fallen around this area, and frequently enact the Rite of Contrition to make up for any taint their poisonous paints might have carried with them.&quot;<br /> <br /> The character has the Rite of Contrition but it has an actual mechanic attached to it. You do it to counteract Renown-Chagrin. But the description is weird in the sense that this character apparently keeps doing graffiti but also thinks that's bad because of the environmental damage the paints are causing. Not only that, but the chances of this character succeeding on this Rite are low. Also, I don't think I would put this character into Chagrin for spray-painting a wall... Especially if the goal of the action is to set up warning-signs for other Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Methinks the writer thought of the olf Contrition which is more RP based.<br /> <br /> Also, WHO is the character doing contrition FOR?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T01:49:07-07:00","id":1533508,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it feels more like a roleplaying-beat. It's more like a personal thing he's doing for himself than this actual Garou-Rite. I don't think you need to fill up that slot for the Rite at character-creation for something like that. Maybe the Rite of Tranquility would work better as something more functional.<br /> <br /> Also, one thing that makes it incongruous with the W5 corebook is the depiction of the older Garou. You'd think they'd go for a nastier portrayal, with the caern going dark and the general situation getting worse for Noble Green. But rather they come off as well-meaning and show dedication to making things better. There's no &quot;Let's exploit the Litany to browbeat young Garou.&quot; as it's suggested in the W5 corebook, for example. Instead, three of the five pre-gens have the Mentor-Background and the Sept-Leader is supportive while when it really matters during the final fight Curbstomp from the rival Pack will help the PCs as best as he can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T02:41:59-07:00","id":1533509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1533508#post1533508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, one thing that makes it incongruous with the W5 corebook is the depiction of the older Garou. You'd think they'd go for a nastier portrayal, with the caern going dark and the general situation getting worse for Noble Green. But rather they come off as well-meaning and show dedication to making things better. There's no &quot;Let's exploit the Litany to browbeat young Garou.&quot; as it's suggested in the W5 corebook, for example. Instead, three of the five pre-gens have the Mentor-Background and the Sept-Leader is supportive while when it really matters during the final fight Curbstomp from the rival Pack will help the PCs as best as he can.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, this gives me the feeling that they COULDN'T actually do the 'all elders suck and there is no structure' setting, because it is very hard to write stories when you've been given no hooks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T03:22:57-07:00","id":1533510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1533509#post1533509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, this gives me the feeling that they COULDN'T actually do the 'all elders suck and there is no structure' setting, because it is very hard to write stories when you've been given no hooks.</div> </div> </div> </div>And by the same token, the pre-gen young Garou PCs don't have this aggressive rebellious streak of &quot;If the Garou-traditions were so goddamn perfect why is Noble Green in such a horrible state?&quot;. The Silent Strider partially blames themselves, the Silver Fang sees themselves as a student of a Garou-hero from the past, the Black Fury thinks wielding the power of Garou allows them to fix things etc. Because in that same way, they <i>couldn't</i> actually go through with that kind of extreme rebellion when at the end of the day the game is still asking players to play Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T11:57:46-07:00","id":1533567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1533510#post1533510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And by the same token, the pre-gen young Garou PCs don't have this aggressive rebellious streak of &quot;If the Garou-traditions were so goddamn perfect why is Noble Green in such a horrible state?&quot;. The Silent Strider partially blames themselves, the Silver Fang sees themselves as a student of a Garou-hero from the past, the Black Fury thinks wielding the power of Garou allows them to fix things etc. Because in that same way, they <i>couldn't</i> actually go through with that kind of extreme rebellion when at the end of the day the game is still asking players to play Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as this is amusing, I have to admit it is also basically making W5 more like the Legacy. When a lot of people who got to W5 got to it BECAUSE they disliked the Legacy.<br /> <br /> It also means that the setting stated in the core is very much not present beyond it.<br /> <br /> That and also, this means that the people wanting to get into W5 after Shattered Nation releases are going to have a core that is USELESS in terms of garou culture. Not to mention returning to the issue where you need to know a lot more than the core to play WtA well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T22:31:47-07:00","id":1533679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1533567#post1533567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As much as this is amusing, I have to admit it is also basically making W5 more like the Legacy. When a lot of people who got to W5 got to it BECAUSE they disliked the Legacy.<br /> <br /> It also means that the setting stated in the core is very much not present beyond it.<br /> <br /> That and also, this means that the people wanting to get into W5 after Shattered Nation releases are going to have a core that is USELESS in terms of garou culture. Not to mention returning to the issue where you need to know a lot more than the core to play WtA well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly I feel this would necessitate a heavy revision of the core book or even release of a WTA 5.5 book in the future if all the renegade supplement is goes agenst the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T01:39:32-07:00","id":1533685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1533567#post1533567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As much as this is amusing, I have to admit it is also basically making W5 more like the Legacy. When a lot of people who got to W5 got to it BECAUSE they disliked the Legacy.<br /> <br /> It also means that the setting stated in the core is very much not present beyond it.<br /> <br /> That and also, this means that the people wanting to get into W5 after Shattered Nation releases are going to have a core that is USELESS in terms of garou culture. Not to mention returning to the issue where you need to know a lot more than the core to play WtA well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think as far as the W5 corebook is concerned, it probably would want STs to focus on this part of the conclusion: &quot;The death of Stitches-the-Soul won\u2019t help with urban decay caused by political apathy but at least it helps people who live in the area by making sNap less acessible.&quot; That's more in line with the whole &quot;The Real Problem with the Garou&quot;-section in the corebook. Make it more like &quot;Look, it's a small victory and you having killed that one bad Garou hasn't really changed the dismal state of the world.&quot;. What brings it then more back to the previous versions is to focus more instead on how a caern gets reclaimed, how other Garou are flocking to the region and how the PC-Pack has now a duty to honor a particular hero of the past from the Garou Nation.<br /> <br /> Also as an aside: At one point it says<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The players\u2019 characters have attained a new position in the local sept. They\u2019re no longer untested cubs but young Garou ready to make their mark!\u200b </div> </div> </div>Damn, wouldn't it be cool to have an in-universe shorthand to describe that, like, you know, how in VtM you have Fledgeling, Neonate and Ancilla as in-universe titles. Here's an idea: You come up with a bunch of in-universe titles and they're like... Ranks. But I'm sure since the W5 corebook only ever distinguishes between Elders (who are bad) and young Garou, no edition of WtA has ever addressed this...<br /> <br /> Instead in W5 you go from untested cub to young Garou to young-ish Garou until you become an Elder yourself. Some real &quot;You either die a hero or you live long enough to see yourself become the villain.&quot;-vibes<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T04:01:21-07:00","id":1533690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1533685#post1533685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead in W5 you go from untested cub to young Garou to young-ish Garou until you become an Elder yourself. Some real &quot;You either die a hero or you live long enough to see yourself become the villain.&quot;-vibes<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />..\u200b<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet with how the adventure panned out it would be more along the line of &quot;the younger generations is finally in a position to lead the garou into a brighter future&quot; since all the pregnes didn't have any problems the garou nation as a whole (the sliver fang is outright stated to be a student of a garou hero)..<br /> <br /> Also the only bad things I can say about the local elders in the adventure as written is them being a mite too passive with the situation. Only for the them to throw they support behind the pregens when they take charge.<br /> <br /> Again it's another thing in this adventure that runs counter to the corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 04-06-2024, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T07:01:25-07:00","id":1533694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1533690#post1533690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yet with how the adventure panned out it would be more along the line of &quot;the younger generations is finally in a position to lead the garou into a brighter future&quot; since all the pregnes didn't have any problems the garou nation as a whole (the sliver fang is outright stated to be a student of a garou hero)..<br /> <br /> Also the only bad things I can say about the local elders in the adventure as written is them being a mite too passive with the situation. Only for the them to throw they support behind the pregens when they take charge.<br /> <br /> Again it's another thing in this adventure that runs counter to the corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's the timeline that's a bit weird. You have the one Pack leaving their caern to attack the ruined hospital, they get killed except for one. That one survivor goes insane (suffers from Hauglosk) and now works together with a Bane-Spirit to manufacture the drug and spread it. Months pass as this happens. Then at some point the Sept Leader is sending out Stormcrow-Spirits to check on the caerns and realizes that this particular one has gone dark. Then a week later she gathers the Garou to choose the PC-Pack for the task of investigating what's going on.<br /> <br /> It's easy to fix, I think. You remove the Stormcrow-Spirit-stuff, you say that the Garou are all busy with taking care of the drug-dealers and various manufactoring-sites while they try to figure out who's passing around the formula for the drug. So the Sept was distracted and at some point the Sept-Leader is like &quot;Hang on, whatever happened to that one Pack? They haven't checked in for a while now...&quot;. Something like that.<br /> <br /> And there's actually yet another thing in where it goes against the corebook: The caern. At the end of the adventure, it's Curbstomp who gets to claim the caern and become its guardian, not the players. They instead (if you pick the extended ending that's supposed to connect to more adventures) witness the Sept-Leader get handed three talismans from that historical Garou-hero Starmantle and it's suggested the Sept-Leader has some task in mind for the PC-Pack in connection with that. But that's weird in the sense that the W5 corebook is very explicit about <i>assuming </i>the PCs will end up managing a caern. And yet here's this golden opportunity to push players into that but instead the adventure deliberately chooses to turn the PCs path away from that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T13:46:00-07:00","id":1533718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1533694#post1533694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And there's actually yet another thing in where it goes against the corebook: The caern. At the end of the adventure, it's Curbstomp who gets to claim the caern and become its guardian, not the players. They instead (if you pick the extended ending that's supposed to connect to more adventures) witness the Sept-Leader get handed three talismans from that historical Garou-hero Starmantle and it's suggested the Sept-Leader has some task in mind for the PC-Pack in connection with that. But that's weird in the sense that the W5 corebook is very explicit about <i>assuming </i>the PCs will end up managing a caern. And yet here's this golden opportunity to push players into that but instead the adventure deliberately chooses to turn the PCs path away from that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> well this adventure seems to partly lead into shartted nation since this supplement is introducing pack types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-26T03:56:39-07:00","id":1534758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1533462#post1533462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like someone might have taken note of online discussions of Hauglosk and how, by the description as written, you can see the impressions of the Swords of Heimdall wall under the hasty wallpapering job.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what would be really stupid? A supplement hastily retconning Hauglosk into a non Rotting varant of a Wyrm corruption.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway moving on is it possible to adapt the adventure into w20 or even Minds eye theatre werewolf or even werewolf the essentials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-26T07:07:06-07:00","id":1534759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1534758#post1534758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know what would be really stupid? A supplement hastily retconning Hauglosk into a non Rotting varant of a Wyrm corruption.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Or an interactive novel where the Cult of Fenris are straight up all neo-nazis with all the iconography that comes with it. <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/WhiteWolfRPG/comments/1cdbfn5/the_new_v5_wta_interactive_novel_came_out_and/\" target=\"_blank\">That'd be absolutely terrible, given the context that we already know about how everything went down behind the scenes.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-26T08:22:26-07:00","id":1534761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1534759#post1534759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or an interactive novel where the Cult of Fenris are straight up all neo-nazis with all the iconography that comes with it. <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/WhiteWolfRPG/comments/1cdbfn5/the_new_v5_wta_interactive_novel_came_out_and/\" target=\"_blank\">That'd be absolutely terrible, given the context that we already know about how everything went down behind the scenes.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>....Wow. Just WOW.<br /> <br /> So now its not even <i>slightly</i> subtext, it is just text...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-26T10:00:37-07:00","id":1534766,"title":"","content":"Because the reddit thread got locked, here is what it said about the fenrir;<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;</i> <div align=\"left\"><i><span style=\"font-family:gg sans\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">They</span></span><span style=\"font-family:gg sans\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">'re straight up neo</span></span><span style=\"font-family:gg sans\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">-nazis</span></span><span style=\"font-family:gg sans\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">. They have swastika and black sun tattoos</span></span><span style=\"font-family:gg sans\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, one wears a shirt of the USA that says </span></span><span style=\"font-family:gg sans\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;Conquered</span></span><span style=\"font-family:gg sans\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, not stolen</span></span><span style=\"font-family:gg sans\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;</span></span><span style=\"font-family:gg sans\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, and they plan to burn down a barn full of liberal punks</span></span></i><br /> </div> <div align=\"left\"><i><span style=\"font-family:gg sans\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">If that wasn't bad enough</span></span><span style=\"font-family:gg sans\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, the Get are best friends with cops who they send to harass and arrest you</span></span><span style=\"font-family:gg sans\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">. You have to spend money to get the cops away from you until you actually kill the Get</span></span>.&quot;</i></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-26T10:47:17-07:00","id":1534770,"title":"","content":"I've bought the game and I'm planning to play it this weekend. I'm planning on writing a review once I'm done. So I guess, I'll see what it's like...<br /> <br /> But with yet another example of linking the Cult of Fenris to Nazism, it's clear: The idea of Get of Fenris=Nazis is still very much alive. And come on, they're really gonna keep doing this... the way they're gonna indicate the evilness of the Cult of Fenris is to make them actual Nazis, not anything Garou-specific... sigh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-26T18:25:49-07:00","id":1534786,"title":"","content":"CoF are supposed to be super gungho about defending/avenging Gaia ( every depiction so far aside) so....isn't a building full of soft left partiers a very low value and nonsense target?*<br /> <br /> *I've only read excerpts so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-26T20:27:23-07:00","id":1534794,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I guess there were too many people saying, &quot;No, the Get aren't <i>literal</i> Nazis&quot; so Paradox felt the need to make it clear that, no, the Get of Fenris really are just Nazis who can turn into Werewolves.<br /> <br /> It's also interesting that, so far, none of the adventures in W5 have involved Black Spirals as the primary villains, but rather the Fenris. So the Fenris are now the intended primary antagonist for the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 04-27-2024, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-26T21:09:10-07:00","id":1534795,"title":"","content":"In other words Karim got everything he wanted....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-26T22:06:58-07:00","id":1534796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1534794#post1534794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I guess there were too many people saying, &quot;No, the Get aren't <i>literal</i> Nazis&quot; so Paradox felt the need to make it clear that, no, the Get of Fenris really are just Nazis who can turn into Werewolves.<br /> <br /> It's also interesting that, so far, none of the adventures in W5 have involved Black Spirals as the primary villains, but rather the Fenris. So the Fenris are now the intended primary antagonist for the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's statement kind of inaccurate since reclamation antag is ( pardon the pun) a lone wolf who got corrupted by a Baine. <br /> <br /> I honestly think that Cof is going to go the way of the black hand sooner rather than later since Renegade seems to be shying away including them in the adventures and I hope they realize that nazi werewolves don't make for a compelling antagonist. I mean they did a 180 on the tone of the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-27T10:48:33-07:00","id":1534812,"title":"","content":"The worst part of this is that it, once more, breaks the firmly stated rule of oWoD; Supernaturals cannot be the cause of IRL events and their drama has to be at least somewhat removed from IRL organizations. Just because it makes it easier to play a pretend game dealing with these things.<br /> <br /> WoD5 clings to real life conflicts and issues to the detriment of its supernatural PCs. A bunch of neo-nazi with cop help harassing squatter punks? That's stuff ANY splat could deal with. The issue isn't at all Werewolf, it just has that coat of paint.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-27T12:46:50-07:00","id":1534815,"title":"","content":"Its so weird to me that the supposed Uberest Garou that ever Ubered are constantly shown relying on human assistance and followers.......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-27T12:48:14-07:00","id":1534816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1534812#post1534812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The worst part of this is that it, once more, breaks the firmly stated rule of oWoD; Supernaturals cannot be the cause of IRL events and their drama has to be at least somewhat removed from IRL organizations. Just because it makes it easier to play a pretend game dealing with these things.<br /> <br /> WoD5 clings to real life conflicts and issues to the detriment of its supernatural PCs. A bunch of neo-nazi with cop help harassing squatter punks? That's stuff ANY splat could deal with. The issue isn't at all Werewolf, it just has that coat of paint.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My biggest question is whats in it for the Coffees?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-27T13:22:01-07:00","id":1534818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1534816#post1534816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My biggest question is whats in it for the Coffees?</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point, I bet what would be in for similar human groups; Trying to look powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-27T13:30:19-07:00","id":1534819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1534818#post1534818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At this point, I bet what would be in for similar human groups; Trying to look powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they're Garou.......its like a bunch of high schoolers trying to look tough by beating up kindergartners + they brought some other young kids ( the cops) to help.....it makes them look pathetic and weak to any other Garou or Spirits watching.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-27T13:31:47-07:00","id":1534820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1534815#post1534815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its so weird to me that the supposed Uberest Garou that ever Ubered are constantly shown relying on human assistance and followers.......</div> </div> </div> </div>It is the same reason you cannot just take out the cops through being a werewolf with supernatural gifts; It starts and ends within human limits. If a regular human cannot scare away cops using Rage, then a garou cannot, either.<br /> <br /> I get the feeling this is because they don't want to abstract these situations at all because they fear the it would be hard to relate to them.<br /> <br /> I mean, look at the text in most WoD5 books, it has this rather &quot;How do you do fellow kids&quot; tone to it, rather than the more general tone of previous editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-27T13:46:36-07:00","id":1534821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1534819#post1534819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But they're Garou.......its like a bunch of high schoolers trying to look tough by beating up kindergartners + they brought some other young kids ( the cops) to help.....it makes them look pathetic and weak to any other Garou or Spirits watching.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing, isn't it? It makes no sense for a bunch of creatures that can become 9-feet of furry blender in an instant. But if the point is not the werewolf but the actions of the neo-nazi on punks, then it makes sense. The werewolf is secondary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-27T16:14:43-07:00","id":1534824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1534820#post1534820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is the same reason you cannot just take out the cops through being a werewolf with supernatural gifts; It starts and ends within human limits. If a regular human cannot scare away cops using Rage, then a garou cannot, either.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Well in the free Rpg <a href=\"https://thelorc.itch.io/what-big-teeth\" target=\"_blank\">What big teeth</a> you can't use your werewolf powers to deal with mundane threats like the police. Of course in that game killing people using your werewolf powers would feed curse and risk turning them grimm (freal werewolf fully succumbed to the curse) and killing people as a human also carries psychological risks...<br /> <br /> Honestly I thought parawolf moved on from IRL events after that International incident or is it just a parawolf thing since the adventure that's the <b>main topic of this thread</b> is written by Renegade and besides the drug distribution sub plot, the main focuses of it on dealing with the bane tanted werewolf and reclaiming the cearn.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 04-29-2024, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-29T16:47:52-07:00","id":1534923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1534786#post1534786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CoF are supposed to be super gungho about defending/avenging Gaia ( every depiction so far aside) so....isn't a building full of soft left partiers a very low value and nonsense target?*<br /> <br /> *I've only read excerpts so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well apparently the underling of the main bad guy agrees since in chapter 9 they offed him because he's wasting time with human politics and not killing banes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-06T10:31:01-07:00","id":1535194,"title":"","content":"There is a metric ton of what I assume is counted as canon material in the BOHN ebook on important subjects ranging from Patron interactions, Tribal History, Sept functions, compositions and positions, ' kinfolk&quot; groups that assist and complicate Garou activities and a whole lot of other subjects......<br /> <br /> ........but unless people pick particular choices in the gamebook they may never know large chunks of it......this seems less than ideal....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-06T12:00:03-07:00","id":1535197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1535194#post1535194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a metric ton of what I assume is counted as canon material in the BOHN ebook on important subjects ranging from Patron interactions, Tribal History, Sept functions, compositions and positions, ' kinfolk&quot; groups that assist and complicate Garou activities and a whole lot of other subjects......<br /> <br /> ........but unless people pick particular choices in the gamebook they may never know large chunks of it......this seems less than ideal....</div> </div> </div> </div>Also do keep in mind that canon seems to be a very fluid category for the current crew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-06T17:59:42-07:00","id":1535204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally pos